and the `inspect` import. Added `_function_path`, which unwraps partials and describes callable instances via `type(func).__call__`. `BackgroundTask` now takes `(name, func)` and sets `self.function`. `add()` no longer does a plugin lookup. Added the read-only `launched` property.\n- **`datasette/app.py`**: added `_tasks()` next to `_threads`, returning `tasks` and `launched`. Each task has `name`, `state`, `function`, `started_at` and `exception` (`repr` or `None`). Added the `/-/tasks(\\.json)?` route right after `/-/threads`, gated by `permissions-debug`. The `add_background_task` docstring now names `.function`.\n- **`docs/introspection.rst`**: new `/-/tasks` section in the `/-/threads` style with an example response. The stability note now also exempts `/-/tasks` as a debug endpoint.\n- **`docs/internals.rst`**: `.plugin` replaced with `.function` in the `BackgroundTask` attribute list.\n\nThings to know:\n\n- I wrote `_tasks` with an explicit loop rather than a comprehension, to keep lines under 88 characters. Black isn't installed in the venv, so I didn't run a formatter.\n- I didn't run the wider test suite. The spec's check was the stop condition. I did grep `datasette`, `tests` and `docs` for leftover `.plugin` and `_resolve_plugin_name` references and found none.\n- `SPEC.md` is untracked and I left it alone. I haven't committed anything.", "ttft_ms": 1610, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 59617, "uuid": "9bc6b84d-7b3b-459d-a9f3-e546517370e5", "ttft_stream_ms": 1533, "time_to_request_ms": 513, "first_content_frame_ms": 1533, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
